# Voice Pipeline — Azure Foundry ONLY

The voice pipeline MUST use the 2-hop architecture:
1. Grok via Azure Foundry Realtime (AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT + AZURE_API_KEY) for TEXT generation
2. Azure TTS Onyx (gpt-4o-mini-tts) for speech synthesis
3. WAV → μ-law conversion → Twilio stream

NEVER use xAI Realtime WebSocket (wss://api.x.ai) for voice. It was tested and:
- Returns HTTP 429 under load
- Cannot handle 8+ concurrent calls
- Was explicitly rolled back on April 6, 2026

The Azure Foundry pipeline handles 200+ concurrent connections.

## Protected Files

- `twilio_grok_xtts_pipeline.py` (max 50 new lines per session)
- Do NOT add xAI direct API calls
- Do NOT add XAI_REALTIME_URL references
- Do NOT add Rex native voice
- Do NOT re-add XAI_API_KEY for WebSocket auth — use AZURE_API_KEY with `api-key` header

## Connection Pattern (Canonical)

```python
ws = await websockets.connect(
    f"wss://{AZURE_OPENAI_ENDPOINT}/openai/realtime?api-version=2024-10-01-preview&deployment={AZURE_OPENAI_DEPLOYMENT}",
    extra_headers={"api-key": AZURE_API_KEY},
)
```

## Enricher Dependencies

- `voice_context_enricher.py` — called at line ~195, injects [STORY JOURNEY] into system prompt
- `voice_crystal_enricher.py` — called at line ~1665, enriches crystals post-call
- Both are pure DB queries, independent of the WebSocket provider
